A Git tag is a permanent bookmark that points to a specific commit in your history.

git tag → lists all tags

git tag V1.0.0 → creates a tag

git show v1.0.0 → shows details of specific tag

git push origin v1.0.0 → push a specific tag

git push origin --tags → Push all local tags at once

