GIT SSH AUTHENTICATION

Git SSH (Secure Shell) authentication is a secure method of connecting your computer to remote repositories (like GitHub) using a matching pair of cryptographic keys.

git ssh -t ed25519 -C "my-email" → prompts us to create a key pair. a private key and a public key

private key - local to system
pubic key - shared to the remote repo

cat ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub → displays public key
 

